    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test in the suite, and it passes. Build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**The behavior:** when a create request sets `sharesHousehold: true` and an existing owner already has the same last name and address, the request is allowed (this bypass already existed in `EnsureUniqueHousehold`), and both the new owner and the matching existing owner(s) are assigned the **same stable `householdId`**, which is returned via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`AssignHousehold.java`** (new function class) \u2014 after `BuildOwner`, when `sharesHousehold` is true and a same-lastName/same-address owner exists, it derives a stable id (`H-` + first 6 bytes of SHA-256 of the normalized `lastName|address`) and assigns it to the new owner while back-filling it onto matching existing owners. Deriving from the household key makes the id identical for every member regardless of creation order. Normalization (trim, collapse whitespace, lowercase) matches `EnsureUniqueHousehold`.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `assignHousehold` step (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `build` and `defaultRegistrationDate`.\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `household_id` column with getter/setter.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `householdId` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` response schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it; `sharesHousehold` stays request-only on `OwnerFields`).\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 ignore `householdId` when mapping from `OwnerFieldsDto` (the request DTO has no such field).\n\n6. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `household_id` column. Tests run on the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so this was required for the column to exist.\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` passes and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
